cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Hatun Doctrine Specification
message: "If you use the Hatun Doctrine Specification, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Lutar
    given-names: Stephen P.
    name-suffix: Jr.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-0110-4173"
    affiliation: "SZL Holdings, Inc."
abstract: >
  The Hatun Doctrine Specification is the constitutional governance schema for
  agentic AI systems in the SZL substrate. It defines machine-checkable JSON
  Schemas for ten governance artifacts: constitution, system-card, risk-report,
  snapshot-fingerprint, behavioral-audit-finding, adversarial-robustness-score,
  coordinated-agent-vulnerability-disclosure, covenant-lift-sample,
  welfare-telemetry-sample, and glasswing-partner-attestation. Each schema is
  enforceable via the companion GitHub Action (tools/github-actions/hatun-doctrine).
  Quechua "hatun" = great, supreme, foundational.
keywords:
  - AI governance
  - JSON Schema
  - constitutional AI
  - agentic systems
  - Lean 4
  - DSSE attestation
  - SZL doctrine
